{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014756-if-you-were-kinfolk","id":1014756,"title":"If you were Kinfolk...?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-09T07:27:39-08:00","id":1014756,"title":"If you were Kinfolk...?","content":"If you were Kinfolk, which Breed of Fera (or Tribe of Garou) would you want to belong to and why? If given a chance, which three Gifts would you want to learn and why? What role would you like to play in the society or your relatives and why?<br /> <br /> I would want to play a Japanese-American Hakken Kinfolk because I like the Hakken Tribe, and I believe that they would want one of their relatives in the US to handle their American investments. I given the opportunity, I would want to learn the Gifts of Dream of a Thousand Cranes, Echoes, and Fair Path because they would help me be an effective business person. My role would be the president of an American subsidiary of a company owned by my Japanese relatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T07:45:56-08:00","id":1014767,"title":"","content":"Glasswalker Kin. My father is a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amateur_radio\" target=\"_blank\">Ham Radio Operator</a> and always had a temper, so I could totally see him being Glasswalker Thuerge or Philodox. His Repeater Group would be a cover for the Glasswalker Sept.<br /> <br /> Being the quiet and rebellious type, I'd probably run off as soon as I knew I wasn't Garou and lived my own life. I'm bad kinfolk, so no gifts for me. My sister inherited his temper, so I imagined she would be the Garou in the family. I could see myself coming back to the Sept after a decade or so for my little Sister though. <br /> <br /> Edit: I looked up the auspices for my family. I would have been a philodox. My father was born during the crescent moon. My sister, the new moon. Her personality fits ragabash. <br /> <br /> This is starting to get frightening. Maybe I really am kinfolk and don't know it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 12-09-2016, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T08:24:32-08:00","id":1014779,"title":"","content":"Not sure about want to be, but my mother's definitely a Shadow Lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T10:03:52-08:00","id":1014816,"title":"","content":"Storytelling was important to both my parents, and family still means a lot to me. My mother's folks are from the Kentucky backwoods and my father's side comes from Berkshire (there are some mouldering ruins that bear the family name). I think Fianna would be a good fit. I like to fix things, so helping out the Garou with mechanical issues would be right up my alley.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T10:33:50-08:00","id":1014829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014756-if-you-were-kinfolk#post1014756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were Kinfolk, which Breed of Fera (or Tribe of Garou) would you want to belong to and why? If given a chance, which three Gifts would you want to learn and why? What role would you like to play in the society or your relatives and why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gurahl Ice Stalker Kinfolk because of their penchant for art and because I like their optimistic approach to life. Kinfolk aren't handed gifts, so no point in picking them. I would be working support and an environmental activist, as well as on call for whatever else is needed. Their goals are virtuous enough that it would be easy enough to throw in time or effort wherever necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T15:39:46-08:00","id":1014973,"title":"","content":"Pre-W20 I'd definitely say Mokole kin, because for one the breed book painted them out to have a great relationship with their changing family members. There was a little bit about the 8th sun and the blurb under the Duty &quot;All are of Gaia&quot; it discussed about how Mokole were typically more understanding...heck under the &quot;reality&quot; of the law it states they see Garou as being rather brutal to their kin. Plus the idea of being related to reptiles is a major plus for me as well (currently I have 9 reptiles and 10 amphibians in my house). &quot;HE'S NOT MY EXOTIC PET, HE'S MY BROTHER!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T16:48:46-08:00","id":1015895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014756-if-you-were-kinfolk?p=1014779#post1014779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure about want to be, but my mother's definitely a Shadow Lord.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel the same way about not WANTING to be... but my mom acts like a black fury... an especialy obnoxious one.<br /> <br /> <br /> which tribe would I want to belong to?<br /> <br /> the silver fangs.<br /> <br /> royal bloodline, wealth, ancient heritage...<br /> <br /> sign me up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T18:51:02-08:00","id":1015933,"title":"","content":"A male Silver Fang Human Kinfolk with Pure Breed 5 is probably going to be the most desired male in the country, even if he is otherwise unremarkable, as he would have a 35% chance of siring a child who likely be Garou on any female Garou, even if she was a Bone Gnawer. He will likely be allowed to breed with anyone he wants until his family can find him a suitable match for marriage, as long as he is discrete, though he may find himself officially delegated to 'entertain' important female Garou or female Human Kinfolk from allied Families and allied Tribes while he is unattached, in order to promote good will within the Garou Nation. By contrast, a female Silver Fang Human Kinfolk with Pure Breed 5 will be discouraged from breeding with the riffraff and will only breed after she is married to the most noble of scions of the Silver Fang Tribe (when she will probably be encouraged to bear at least six children because an average of two of them will likely be Garou).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:56:13-08:00","id":1016613,"title":"","content":"Being kinfolk to the Nuwisha or Kitsune might not be too bad. They both seem like groups that would have a fairly high appreciation for their kinfolk, and due to their positions would view their own kinfolk with a bit more of an equitable relationship, plus they tend not to have very close relations with their kin<br /> <br /> Also, maybe a Glasswalker kinfolk would be okay. Of the various tribes they seem like the one who would be more willing to offer some kind of quid pro quo arrangement for a kinfolk's help, rather than just showing up out of the blue and demanding you drop everything to assist them because it's your &quot;duty.&quot; <br /> <br /> But I I definitely wouldn't want to be Bone Gnawer or Ratkin kinfolk - you know, the kind of group that's likely to show up on your doorstep and crash at your place for a couple of weeks or make you help them out in performing potentially illegal activity (like say, building pipebombs to blow up the local fast food restaurant). <br /> <br /> Still, if push came to shove I don't know if I'd really want to be a Kinfolk in the first place. In a lot of ways it seems like more trouble than it's worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T10:07:06-08:00","id":1016618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014756-if-you-were-kinfolk?p=1016613#post1016613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still, if push came to shove I don't know if I'd really want to be a Kinfolk in the first place. In a lot of ways it seems like more trouble than it's worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't make sense to me. If you are a kinfolk, you should at least have some idea about the war for Gaia. Your cousins/siblings/whatever might not be the most pleasant creatures, but they are still going to protect you and yours and they fight to the defend the world. If you were in WW2 and you were required to do your part for the war, would you gripe? Maybe a little, but you know that your sacrifices are small compared to those putting their lives on the line to confront evil head-on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T10:56:33-08:00","id":1016645,"title":"","content":"Kinfolk are basically forced to fight in a war that they never asked for, and they don't really receive any of the blessings that Fera or Werewolves do. They have to make all kinds of sacrifices and do a lot of shit work and they don't really get any real rewards in exchange except, perhaps, to be used as breeding stock (yay?)<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd rather be able to live a life where I had the ability to live the life I want, marry whomever I wanted, and pursue the lifestyle that I wanted, and not have to worry about a bunch of shapechanging cousins knocking on my door one day telling me that I have to drop everything to help them do X (probably without compensation) because it's my duty, and if I refuse there will be <i>consequences</i>.<br /> <br /> I think in a lot of ways Kinfolk get one of the shortest straws in the World of Darkness, to the point where being a normal human would quite honestly be preferable. There's a small handful of tribes and Fera who treat their kinfolk with respect and allow their kinfolk to have the power to live their own lives, but for most they view Kinfolk as a valuable resource and treat them more like servants or, at best, second-class family members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T11:20:49-08:00","id":1016657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014756-if-you-were-kinfolk?p=1016645#post1016645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinfolk are basically forced to fight in a war that they never asked for, and they don't really receive any of the blessings that Fera or Werewolves do. They have to make all kinds of sacrifices and do a lot of shit work and they don't really get any real rewards in exchange except, perhaps, to be used as breeding stock (yay?)<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd rather be able to live a life where I had the ability to live the life I want, marry whomever I wanted, and pursue the lifestyle that I wanted, and not have to worry about a bunch of shapechanging cousins knocking on my door one day telling me that I have to drop everything to help them do X (probably without compensation) because it's my duty, and if I refuse there will be <i>consequences</i>.<br /> <br /> I think in a lot of ways Kinfolk get one of the shortest straws in the World of Darkness, to the point where being a normal human would quite honestly be preferable. There's a small handful of tribes and Fera who treat their kinfolk with respect and allow their kinfolk to have the power to live their own lives, but for most they view Kinfolk as a valuable resource and treat them more like servants or, at best, second-class family members.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kinfolk get the shittiest lot in WoD, but they are also the most needed by their Supernatural relatives. <br /> <br /> Being a Garou is tough. You can't interact with Humans real well. You are waging a deadly war where very few of the cubs at your Rite of Passage are alive by Rank 3. When your pack mates die around you, you need your non-garou kin to keep your grounded. Or else you could lose yourself to the rage. <br /> <br /> I think this is why Glasswalkers are so... reasonable with their kin. As the tribe closest to humans, Glasswalkers understand how much they need kinfolk. Yes, they are still rage filled Warriors of Gaia, but they are going to try to give back to their kin when they can. Money and Contacts don't seem much after your Ahroun cousin knocks you around, but it better than nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T11:27:36-08:00","id":1016661,"title":"","content":"Well, actually, everything in WtA fights the war, whether they know it or not. The people who work for most corporations fight for the Wyrm by speading environmental degradation and labor exploitation across the world or they fight for the Weaver by spreading consumerism or propoganda. The people working for most governments are fighting for either the Weaver or the Wyrm. It is the rare human who is fighting for Gaia or the Wyld, and they are outnumbered hundreds to one by the people unwittingly fighting for the Weaver or the Wyrm. <br /> <br /> At least the Kinfolk know that they are involved in a war, though I am sure that they wish they would be given the resources to let them go down fighting, rather than have them begging for help from their kin. I am actually thinking of running a Kinfolk campaign soon where the Kinfolk are as capable as the Dhampyr of KotE, just to see how capable Kinfolk would work. While they will not be as awesome as their Fera relatives, I am sure that it will be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:01:51-08:00","id":1016670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014756-if-you-were-kinfolk?p=1016645#post1016645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinfolk are basically forced to fight in a war that they never asked for, and they don't really receive any of the blessings that Fera or Werewolves do. They have to make all kinds of sacrifices and do a lot of shit work and they don't really get any real rewards in exchange except, perhaps, to be used as breeding stock</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't really get a choice, and it isn't the Garou who are making that choice, either. I think a lot of Garou would want to sit out of that was an option (some do, usually Bone-Gnawer rabble). The situation isn't like the Garou are drafting you to fight in a war against your will; it is more akin to the Nazis suddenly rolling into your hometown and you have the choice between fighting them or collaborating. Neither is going to be 'fun' but at least one will let you die with a clean conscience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014756-if-you-were-kinfolk?p=1016645#post1016645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I'd rather be able to live a life where I had the ability to live the life I want, marry whomever I wanted, and pursue the lifestyle that I wanted, and not have to worry about a bunch of shapechanging cousins knocking on my door one day telling me that I have to drop everything to help them do X (probably without compensation) because it's my duty, and if I refuse there will be <i>consequences</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>In WtA, duty is one of the few reasons why the Wyrm hasn't already won. Fera and their human kin fight against the Wyrm, and if they had this outlook you are espousing, Gaia would already be dead (and the game wouldn't even work). The idea is that the Apocalypse War doesn't allow you to fuck off and do your own thing. If you didn't have your cousins coming around, you could easily end up as BSD bait or fomori chow.<br /> <br /> Even if there was not the threat of the enemy destroying you directly, if there was a struggle for the soul of the world and the fate of all things, and you knew about it, how could you just say 'meh, got mine?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 12-13-2016, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:02:59-08:00","id":1016672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014756-if-you-were-kinfolk?p=1016670#post1016670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if there was not the threat of the enemy destroying you directly, if there was a struggle for the soul of the world, and you knew about it, how could you just say 'meh, got mine?'</div> </div> </div> </div>This. So much this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:20:04-08:00","id":1016678,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of people who would have trouble with Kinfolk expectations, especially in conjunction with the sexual demands of helping to provide offspring for the War, but also in many other ways as well. There are a few tribes and Fera breeds that are okay with allowing Kinfolk to have a fair amount of freedom in choosing how to live their lives (as I mentioned in my first post), but many tribes don't care what Kinfolk want, and you'll see those Kinfolk stuck in oppressive, unhappy situations because of their &quot;duty&quot; to their tribes.<br /> <br /> In comparison, it's not like there's a post-apocalyptic environment in Earth with a fomori around every corner .The vast, vast majority of humans never have any encounter with monsters and live perfectly normal lives. In fact, when Kinfolk do face supernatural threats, it's most likely caused because of the fact that they're Kinfolk in the first place - it's not just a coincidence that there's a Black Spiral Dancer breaking in their front door, that Dancer is there looking for a kinfolk.<br /> <br /> So I would not be surprised if many Kinfolk go to sleep at night fervently wishing they had just been born as regular humans and bemoaning a fate that forces them to live lives that, had they had the choice, they never would have agreed to. Given a choice, I would certainly not choose to be in their shoes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:51:30-08:00","id":1016690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014756-if-you-were-kinfolk?p=1016678#post1016678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In comparison, it's not like there's a post-apocalyptic environment in Earth with a fomori around every corner .</div> </div> </div> </div>This is literally what the Garou and the other Fera are fighting to prevent. You are so focused on the fact that some kinfolk are treated badly that you seem to be ignoring the planet-scale atrocity that would happen if they and their shifter families weren't fighting to stop the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> I feel like you and I are saying the same thing over and over. I am not trying to talk past you, but what a character wants takes a backseat to what needs to be done to prevent that post-apocalyptic hellscape from becoming reality. Freedom is overrated, if that freedom ends up leading you and your people to Malfeas. Like Aya Tari said, most humans are the unwitting pawns of the Weaver or Wyrm. The 'bad guys' of WtA want you to do nothing, to blithely continue consuming while spiritual rot overtakes the earth.<br /> <br /> If you are in WtA, you don't get the luxury of sitting out of the fight. You have to pick a side, and even if being a kinfolk isn't 'fun' it is still right, considering the alternatives. That is what duty is all about, doing something necessary even when it isn't fun or pleasant.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T13:16:30-08:00","id":1016703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014756-if-you-were-kinfolk?p=1016690#post1016690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are in WtA, you don't get the luxury of sitting out of the fight. You have to pick a side, and even if being a kinfolk isn't 'fun' it is still right, considering the alternatives. That is what duty is all about, doing something necessary even when it isn't fun or pleasant.</div> </div> </div> </div>My earlier statement was, if I had the choice, I'd just as soon not be a Kinfolk. I'd rather, oh, I don't know, be a normal person on the real planet Earth than a kinfolk in the World of Darkness (and to be fair, there are a lot of other things in the World of Darkness that I would prefer not to be if given the choice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) I mean, if someone asked, &quot;Which type of Fomori would you rather to be,&quot; I'd probably say, &quot;Well maybe this one, but if given the choice I'd prefer not be a Fomori in the first place.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is kind of where I'm approaching Kinfolk from. They get a pretty raw deal in many respects. I'm certain there are a lot (especially from the more oppressive tribes) who curse the fact that they were born kinfolk. There's a couple of tribes and breeds who try to work with their Kinfolk but for many, Kinfolk are viewed more as a resource to be exploited. And I can safely say that, if given the choice, that's not really the kind of life I would prefer to live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T14:55:53-08:00","id":1016756,"title":"","content":"I do not know if they get a worse deal than ghouls or revenants, and I think that all of the possessed except for the kami get a worse deal. Of the other minor Shadow Folk, the Rom were nearly annihilated by the Nazis and are still oppressed in most nations, the kinain have to depend on the glamour of their kin to even remember why they are so screwed in life, and hunters are nothing more than speed bumps for practically any competent major supernatural. I guess being a sorcerer can be good, as long as the Mages do not pull you into their insanity, and the dhampyr of KotE have it good until their parents come knocking, but life sucks in cWoD for everyone except the bad guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T16:19:20-08:00","id":1016793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014756-if-you-were-kinfolk?p=1016703#post1016703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Which type of Fomori would you rather to be,&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Freakfeet. <br /> <br /> The answer is Freakfeet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-