lose their connection to the Qualmi? Or would it grow stronger with every passing generation as they kept from outcrossing with anyone who they considered outsiders?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T19:29:12-08:00","id":1016871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014756-if-you-were-kinfolk?p=1016861#post1016861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, just out of curiosity, does anyone know how many generations a family can be Kinfolk without new influxes of Fera blood to maintain the bloodline? I mean, could you have a group of Kinfolk, let us say the Innu of Labrador, who could continue to pop out new Qualmi every generation without having any Qualmi breed back in? If the entire population of 3,000 started as Qualmi Kinfolk, how long would it take them to lose their connection to the Qualmi? Or would it grow stronger with every passing generation as they kept from outcrossing with anyone who they considered outsiders?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say kin folk to kin folk will breed more kin. Kin folk to normal human would start to dilute the bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I wri